%% Successful loadDocument sequence
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber

  actor Caller as Application code
  participant Codec as CodecBoundary
  participant API as CanvasEditPort
  participant Runtime as RuntimeRoot
  participant Stager as Staged load boundary
  participant Store as DocumentStoreKernel
  participant Selection as SelectionKernel
  participant Interaction as InteractionEngine
  participant Projection as DocumentProjectionCache
  participant Spatial as SpatialKernel
  participant Resources as ResourceKernel
  participant Frame as FrameEngine
  participant Signals as Public state/effects

  opt caller starts from schema v1 JSON
    Caller->>Codec: decodeCanvasDocument / decodeCanvasDocumentFromJson
    Codec->>Codec: parse schemaVersion 1 and validate known fields
    Codec->>Codec: validate resources, element ids, references, limits, and metadata
    Codec-->>Caller: immutable CanvasDocument DTO with CanvasMetadata
    Note over Codec,Store: Decode materializes only a public DTO and has no runtime or store side effects.
  end

  Caller->>API: loadDocument(document)
  API->>Runtime: delegate loadDocument(document)
  Runtime->>Runtime: reject disposed runtime before mutation
  Runtime->>Store: read current committed identity, document revisions, and id admission state
  Store-->>Runtime: current committed snapshot remains installed
  Runtime->>Selection: read current selectionRevision
  Selection-->>Runtime: current selected ids remain installed

  Runtime->>Stager: validate public CanvasDocument
  Stager->>Stager: verify DTO invariants, limits, duplicate ids, resource references, and frozen metadata
  Runtime->>Stager: prepare full document replacement from DTO and current snapshot
  Stager->>Stager: materialize compact tables, resource descriptors, order, meta, and id generator floor
  Stager-->>Runtime: PreparedDocumentLoad replacement payload
  Note over Runtime,Store: No interaction interrupt, preview clear, cache eviction, repaint, public state publication, or store mutation occurs before preparation succeeds.

  Runtime->>Interaction: success-only interrupt active interaction
  Interaction->>Interaction: cancel active gesture and clear preview
  Interaction->>Interaction: bump previewRevision if preview was active
  Interaction-->>Runtime: preview cleared and preview signal queued until install
  Note over Interaction,Signals: Preview state may be cleared before install, but no public state is published before the committed replacement is installed.

  Runtime->>Store: install PreparedDocumentLoad document payload atomically
  Runtime->>Selection: clear selection in same runtime result
  Store->>Store: replace compact committed tables and id admission in one commit boundary
  Selection->>Selection: clear selected ids and increment selectionRevision if needed
  Store->>Store: assign new committed identity
  Store->>Store: increment controllerEpoch and document/structural/bounds/visual/projection/resource revisions inside the install
  Note over Store: Store state is committed tables and revision state, not a live CanvasDocument DTO.
  Note over Runtime,Selection: Selection clear is not a public post-install mutation; it is part of the same atomic runtime result.
  Store-->>Runtime: committed replacement revision facts and installed persisted camera
  Selection-->>Runtime: committed selection revision facts
  Runtime->>Runtime: initialize runtime view camera from installed persisted document camera

  Runtime->>Interaction: committed load installed with updated epoch and revisions
  Interaction->>Interaction: clear pointer normalization and pending tap history
  Store->>Projection: evict public document projection by projectionRevision
  Runtime->>Spatial: rebuild full spatial index from replacement tables
  Runtime->>Resources: clear image resolve cache for replaced descriptors
  Runtime->>Frame: reset replacement-scoped paint, static, text, path, and stroke caches
  Frame->>Frame: schedule main repaint for replacement document
  Interaction->>Frame: schedule overlay repaint for cleared preview

  Runtime->>Signals: publish one CanvasRuntimeState after install, including required viewCamera revision and preview cleanup revision if changed
  Note over Signals: loadDocument emits no CanvasActionCommitted event.
  Runtime-->>API: loadDocument complete
  API-->>Caller: return after post-install effects are scheduled and the state listener is notified
